Well I've cleared out down to the viberating square.  I left the
wizard's tower alone, although I did check out the fake tower (and
almost steped on the magic portal).

Anyway to recap what's happened since the sacfest.  I headed back out
of the mines.  I wanted to finsh remapping the levels lost by the
mindflayer.  The rogue level proved to be a problem. An L appeared and
promptly summoned some nasties, including a MMF.  Yep you guest it, I
had my brain eaten again.  Also lost my pet MMF. _Then_ I thought about
Magicbane and the E-word.  I ended up charming most of the things it
summoned.  Chased him up three levels each time fighting off a new
batch of summoned nasties..  Then I got the bright idea, to use the
blessed scrolls of genocide I had.  L and h are now gone!  Whoohoo!  A
potion of gain ability seemed to restore all of the lost intellegence
points.

With 10 new pets (a bunch of J's and D's with some things like z's
mixed in). I re-remaped the levels.  It wasn't until I got to DL10 that
I thought, gosh you've got magic mapping.  Made a stop at an alter I
forgot about (just above the Ft entrance).  Had a mini sacfest.  Then
all my pets seemed to become confused from hunger.  Ooops forgot to
feed them.  Made a bunch more things for them to eat, but not before
half of them were killed.  I did have some fun with three dishwashers
and one potion of gain level, brought me to level 30! I also
rediscoverd a sink and got a ring out of it.  Guess what it was?  Well
after polymorphing it, it was a blessed ring of free action!

I'm not sure exactly how, but by time I got back to the castle (there
was some thunder in the distance, so I'm sure it was my fault), I was
down to just two pets (a J and D). Then I walked into the moat without
the ring of levitation.  Oh no no no no!  Luckily I survived. I headed
down and I had just enought gold to buy more protection from the priest
of molloch.  Alas, my J and D got there before me and the priest has
gone off for his reward/punishment before Moloch (exactly how bad is it
to #pray or #offer stuff to Molloch??).

The next level was very easy. One magic missle or a whack with
magicbane and my enemies fell.  Then came Asmodeus.  Not so easy, but
between me and my pets we prevailed.  Then came what I guess was
Jublex's swamp.  He's lost in the mines somewhere.  Too many green
slimes on this level for my piece of mind.   More mazes and then
Baalzebub.  He was a lot like Asmo, but seemed easier.  If I had not
forgotten to eat (and fainted) I would have taken him out and stil be
within 10hp of max.  As it was I still had over 200.

Finally found Vlad's tower.  That was fairly easy.  D & J took him out
before I even finished with the first V in the alcoves.  Found three
spellbooks, none terribly useful.  The throne vanished without doing
anything good or bad for me.

At this point I #invoked the eye and headed for the Ft. (near my stash
and an alter, and still full of food which I was starting to need).
However my stupid J was still eating something and got left.  I quickly
hurried back down after eating and refreshing some spells. The J was
still tame when I found him.

Heading down below Vlad's I came to an abandoned town with Orcus.  He
was much like Baalzebub only easier!?!  In the graveyard, there was a
corpse of a wizard named Jove. More mazes followed.  Then I saw what I
think is the top of the Wizard's tower (there was a bee hive somewhere
on this level but I couldn't get to it). The next two levels had
something similar.

More mazes and what I think was the Fake Tower.  The first one had a
magic portal in the middle, which I didn't step on (I assume it leads
into the real tower).  The 2nd one had a horrible elf lord with an
amulet of reflection.

Not far below, I came to a level without a down stairs.  I found a
square which said "You feel a strange viberation under your feet"
Bingo?

So next is to do the Wizard's tower.  Get the book.  Go back to the
square.  apply the candles to the holder. apply the holder.  ring the
bell and read the book.   Find the High Priest, avoid a bunch of lava,
and the Wizard (can I get protection from the HP first?)  The first
priest of Molloch had all 60k+ of gold and I was thinking of lugging
that down and using that (it's extremely heavy is the only problem).

Anyway I take the amulet from the high priest and run like crazy back
up to lvl 1.  As i understand it the Eye stops working once I get the
amulet right?

Above DL1 are the planes and this is what I've figured out from the
spoilers...
Earth - expect another fight with the wizard. Be glad I've got the dig
spell and tons of wands of digging.  The magic portal is in open space
somewhere.

Air - Keep that ring of leviation on!  The portal is somewhere on the
level

Fire - Hope everything is fireproof.  Keep that ring of levitation on!
The poral is somewhere on the level.

Water - this sounds like a really awful level.  I'm pretty sure I'm
going to need some more info before attempting this level.  The portal
is in an air pocket and moves with the pocket.  How do I get between
air pockets?  I think once I had a ring of water breathing or
something.

Astral - make sure i get the Angel pet (guess I need to #offer stuff at
the last alter before leaving the dungeon).  Hope I avoid Death,
Famine, and Pestilence.  I'm pretty sure I need more info on this one
too..

